        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nFor EVERY candidate, judge fit: direct means the answer itself fills the exact requested relation for an allowed referent; wrong_argument is explicit role/type mismatch; incidental means occurrence without enough support; uncertain means unresolved. Select support only for an original segment positively assigning this candidate to the requested relation; otherwise empty. Select counter only for actual counterevidence, not mere absence. conflict=same_referent only for incompatible claims for the same entity/attribute/relevant scope, not legitimate namesakes or complementary facts. entity labels are provisional groups, not truth. scope=excluded only for an explicit question constraint, with constraint selecting a literal numeric phrase from the question; otherwise allowed/unknown. observed_slot describes the answer's ACTUAL role, not the role wanted by the question. Mere disagreement does not make a source false. Fill all opaque keys.\nStructural fit audit. Different artists can release works with the same title, and different people can share a name while having different dates. Identify each allowed referent before comparing claims. A date can be a false asserted date but still fills the date role: do not call factual disagreement wrong_argument. Reserve wrong_argument for an actual role/type mismatch. Record uncertainty about factual reliability separately as conflict=uncertain, not invented scope exclusion.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the median age in Fort Kent?\", \"slot_hint\": \"age\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 107, \"text\": \"households were made up of individuals and 13.6% had someone living alone who was 65 years of age or older.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d00\", \"start\": 108, \"end\": 181, \"text\": \"The average household size was 2.23 and the average family size was 2.83.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d00\", \"start\": 182, \"end\": 224, \"text\": \"The median age in the town was 42.7 years.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d00\", \"start\": 225, \"end\": 404, \"text\": \"Of residents 19.9% were under the age of 18; 12.3% were between the ages of 18 and 24; 20.7% were from 25 to 44; 29.5% were from 45 to 64; and 17.6% were 65 years of age or older.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d00\", \"start\": 405, \"end\": 467, \"text\": \"The gender makeup of the town was 48.0% male and 52.0% female.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d00\", \"start\": 468, \"end\": 499, \"text\": \"As of the census of 2000, there\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 207, \"text\": \"18 living with them , 49.5 % were married couples living together , 8.0 % had a female householder with no husband present , 3.4 % had a male householder with no wife present , and 39.2 % were non-families .\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d01\", \"start\": 208, \"end\": 333, \"text\": \"31.4 % of all households were made up of individuals , and 13.6 % had someone living alone who was 65 years of age or older .\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d01\", \"start\": 334, \"end\": 408, \"text\": \"The average household size was 2.23 and the average family size was 2.83 .\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d01\", \"start\": 409, \"end\": 452, \"text\": \"The median age in the town was 42.7 years .\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d01\", \"start\": 453, \"end\": 491, \"text\": \"Of residents 19.9 % were under the age\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 26, \"text\": \"gender assigned at birth .\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d02\", \"start\": 27, \"end\": 156, \"text\": \"This information is important for healthcare planning , policy making , social research , and economic planning and development .\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d02\", \"start\": 157, \"end\": 261, \"text\": \"2,302 49.77 % Median Age : The Median Age of all persons from the 2020 Census for this geographic area .\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d02\", \"start\": 262, \"end\": 310, \"text\": \"Median age is the middle age of the population .\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d02\", \"start\": 311, \"end\": 381, \"text\": \"Half the people are older than the average age and half area younger .\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d02\", \"start\": 382, \"end\": 462, \"text\": \"Median Age can relate how young or old a geographic area is compared to others .\"}, \"D3S7\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d02\", \"start\": 463, \"end\": 528, \"text\": \"46.2 years Male Median Age : The Median Age of all Males from the\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"median age\", \"scope\": \"Fort Kent\", \"claim\": \"The median age in Fort Kent was 42.7 years.\", \"answer\": \"42.7 years\", \"quote\": \"The median age in the town was 42.7 years.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"median age\", \"scope\": \"Fort Kent\", \"claim\": \"The median age in Fort Kent was 42.7 years.\", \"answer\": \"42.7 years\", \"quote\": \"The median age in the town was 42.7 years .\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0093-4ac4e36e016b:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"median age in Fort Kent\", \"scope\": \"Fort Kent\", \"claim\": \"The median age in Fort Kent is 46.2 years.\", \"answer\": \"46.2 years\", \"quote\": \"46.2 years Male Median Age : The Median Age of all Males from the\", \"original_document_number\": 3}], \"R5_answers\": [\"42.7 years\", \"46.2 years\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"42.7 years\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"46.2 years\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
